# Developer's Quickstart Guide for Ages of Arda Cursor Rules

Welcome to the Ages of Arda project! This quickstart guide will help you get up and running with our Cursor Rules System, which provides intelligent guidance, consistent coding standards, and research protocols for our Tolkien-inspired game.

## 1. Initial Setup (5 minutes)

### Verify Rules Installation

First, check that the cursor rules are properly installed in your environment:

```powershell
# From the project root
Test-Path .cursor/rules
```

If the rules directory is missing, clone it from the project repository:

```powershell
git clone https://github.com/ages-of-arda/cursor-rules.git .cursor/rules
```

### Configure MCP Integration

For advanced AI assistance, set up the Model Context Protocol servers:

1. Ensure you have `.cursor/mcp.json` configured correctly
2. Store your API keys securely:

```powershell
# Initialize secure credential storage
python .cursor/rules/memory-bank/credential-manager.py init

# Store your API keys
python .cursor/rules/memory-bank/credential-manager.py store BRAVE_SEARCH_API_KEY
python .cursor/rules/memory-bank/credential-manager.py store TAVILY_API_KEY

# Update MCP configuration with secure credentials
python .cursor/rules/memory-bank/credential-manager.py update-mcp
```

## 2. Understanding the Core Principles (10 minutes)

The Ages of Arda Cursor Rules system is built on five core principles:

1. **Contextual Intelligence** - Rules are applied based on file type and content
2. **Tolkien Fidelity** - Ensuring accuracy to Tolkien's works is paramount
3. **Technical Excellence** - Consistent, high-quality code is non-negotiable
4. **Knowledge Integration** - All knowledge flows through connected systems
5. **Self-Healing** - The system continuously improves itself

Read the complete description in [purpose.mdc](../.cursor/rules/purpose.mdc).

